<div id="2026-09-02-schema-compare-connection-selection" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-02 — Fix schema-compare: table side disappearing + "Add to Result" DDL failure</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What (1) — table side vanished.</strong> The schema-compare field page (<code>/admin/schema_compare/server/&lt;group&gt;/db/&lt;db&gt;/table/&lt;table&gt;</code>) intermittently rendered with only the Result side — live DB/table columns missing ("0 match · N result-only"). The display actions picked a connection with a single <code>grep</code> over the group's connections and used <em>whichever came first in hash order</em>. Groups contain dead rows (placeholder credentials such as <code>YOUR_BACKUP_USERNAME</code>, offline hosts, wrong-port fallbacks), so the page nondeterministically bound to a dead connection: <code>get_connection()</code> returned undef, the column list came back empty, and the table side silently vanished. It appeared to "break" on reload (or after an unrelated failed action) even though nothing had changed.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix (1).</strong> Added <code>_pick_live_connection()</code>: walks a group's connections in priority order and returns the first handle that actually connects. Wired into <code>schema_compare_table</code> (field view) and <code>schema_compare_database</code> (table list) — the same flaw existed in both. Verified: 18/18 runs render both sides (previously failing ~2 in 3); the database drill-down lists 216 tables.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What (2) — "Add to Result" failed.</strong> The action died with <code>Failed to connect to database 'ency' for DDL via admin user ''</code>. Two causes: (a) the dedicated admin connection <code>db_production_mysql_admin</code> cannot authenticate, and only <code>db_production_mysql</code> (priority 1, <code>comserv_app</code>) connects, so a DDL-only path had nothing to bind to; (b) <code>_get_fresh_dbh</code> tried to override credentials via <code>$remote_db-&gt;config()</code>, but <code>RemoteDB::get_connection()</code> calls <code>_load_config()</code> internally, which reloads config from disk and <em>discards</em> the override — so the swap never took effect and only produced misleading errors.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix (2).</strong> Removed the ineffective credential swap. <code>_get_fresh_dbh</code> now uses <code>_pick_live_connection()</code>, so it uses a connection that actually connects instead of insisting on an admin DDL handle. This is safe for its read-only callers: <code>get_ency_table_schema</code> (used by "Add to Result") only reads metadata via <code>DESCRIBE</code> / <code>information_schema</code> / <code>SHOW INDEX</code> and never runs DDL. Its failure message now also lists every connection tried plus the real DBI error instead of an empty <code>admin user ''</code>. Verified: <code>_get_fresh_dbh</code> connects, and <code>get_ency_table_schema('inventory_items')</code> returns all 43 columns; the generated Result file content (4635 bytes) and target path resolve correctly.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What (3) — "Add to Result" failed for a field NOT in the Result file.</strong> Clicking "Add to Result" for a field missing from the Result file died with <code>Could not locate field 'selling_price' in result file '...'</code>. Both "Update Result" and "Add to Result" post to <code>/schema-comparison/sync_table_to_result</code> → <code>update_result_field_from_table</code>, but that function only ever called <code>_replace_result_field_block()</code>, which returns undef when the field is absent — so an ADD had no insertion path and died with a replace-only error message.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix (3).</strong> Added <code>_insert_result_field_block()</code>: when the field is not present, it locates the <code>add_columns( ... )</code> block by paren counting and appends the new entry before its closing paren, adding the separating comma only when needed and leaving every existing field untouched. <code>update_result_field_from_table</code> now tries replace first, then insert, and only dies (with a clear message) if the <code>add_columns</code> block itself cannot be found. Verified on a scratch copy of <code>InventoryItem.pm</code>: insert succeeds, other fields preserved, and the result passes <code>perl -c</code> — which is exactly the gate <code>_write_result_file_safe</code> enforces before writing.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What (4) — DECIMAL sizes written incorrectly.</strong> Adding <code>selling_price</code> (a <code>decimal(10,2)</code>) wrote <code>size =&gt; 10,2,</code> into the Result file. The DB parser returns the size as the scalar string <code>"10,2"</code>, not an array ref, so the <code>ref($sz) eq 'ARRAY'</code> check failed and the plain-scalar branch emitted bare-list syntax. That parses (so <code>perl -c</code> passes) but silently sets <code>size</code> to <code>10</code> with a stray <code>2</code>, losing the scale. Fixed: sizes are now normalized — <code>"p,q"</code> becomes <code>[p, q]</code>, plain integers stay scalars, and any other shape is quoted so bare-list syntax can never be emitted again. The already-written <code>InventoryItem.pm</code> entry was corrected to <code>size =&gt; [10, 2]</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/SchemaComparison.pm</code> (<code>_pick_live_connection</code> and <code>_insert_result_field_block</code> new; <code>schema_compare_table</code>, <code>schema_compare_database</code>, <code>_get_fresh_dbh</code>, <code>update_result_field_from_table</code> updated), <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Accounting/InventoryItem.pm</code> (<code>selling_price</code> added, size corrected), changelog fragment.</p>
</div>
